WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.775
First: in a Global Secure Access
outage, what keeps users working?

3
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:10.710
The answer is b: Microsoft's
break-glass scripts that switch the

4
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.250
policies to report-only, rehearsed
and recorded in the contingency plan.

5
00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:19.050
Turning signaling off first
would block users, not save them.

6
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.300
Second: which data planes do
universal tenant restrictions reach?

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.463
The answer is b: the
authentication plane and the

8
00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:30.100
Microsoft Graph data plane,
not SharePoint or Exchange.

9
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:35.060
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
